            name: "amount",
            value: 32,
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_21",
        on: "moveto",
        once: false,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "filter",
            side: 1,
            x: 26,
            y: 35,
          },
          {
            tag: "filter_condition",
            children: [
              {
                tag: "predicate",
                name: "wml_filter",
                unit: "$unit_moved_id",
                filter: "%7B%22tag%22%3A%22event%22%2C%22attributes%22%3A%7B%22name%22%3A%22moveto%22%2C%22first_time_only%22%3A%22no%22%7D%2C%22children%22%3A%5B%7B%22tag%22%3A%22message%22%2C%22attributes%22%3A%7B%22speaker%22%3A%22narrator%22%2C%22message%22%3A%22%E2%80%95%20%20The%20Contest%20of%20the%20Automata%20%20%E2%80%95%5Cn%5CnThere%20was%20a%20rumbling%20in%20the%20distance.%20Puffs%20of%20smoke%20rose%20from%20beyond%20the%20horizon.%20Then%20slowly%20they%20appeared%2C%20two%20hulking%20metal%20champions.%5Cn%5CnThe%20drake%20automaton%20came%20first%20into%20view%2C%20as%20it%20was%20the%20swifter%20of%20the%20two.%20It%20bore%20a%20vague%20likeness%20to%20a%20%3Ci%3Edrakekin%3C%2Fi%3E%2C%20yet%20wingless%2C%20tailless.%20Below%20its%20four%20legs%20were%20rollers%20in%20place%20of%20feet.%20It%20breathed%20a%20menacing%20black%20smoke%20as%20its%20metal%20shell%20gleamed%20like%20golden%20sunlight.%5Cn%5CnThen%20the%20%3Ci%3Ecraftling%3C%2Fi%3E%20automaton%20came%20into%20view.%20Like%20its%20creators%2C%20it%20was%20smaller%2C%20slower.%20The%20rollers%20that%20carried%20it%20were%20covered%20by%20curious%20metal%20feet%20that%20turned%20to%20meet%20the%20ground%20as%20it%20went%20along.%20It%20breathed%20a%20fair%2C%20nigh%20cloudlike%20smoke.%5Cn%5CnThe%20automata%20took%20their%20places%20in%20the%20arena%2C%20facing%20each%20other.%20Their%20inner%20toolworks%20clamored%20ceaselessly.%20The%20call%20was%20given%20to%20begin%20the%20duel.%5Cn%5CnWith%20a%20deafening%20shriek%2C%20the%20drake%20automaton%20spat%20out%20walls%20of%20flame%2C%20as%20it%20lurched%20ahead.%20Even%20the%20sand%20seemed%20to%20burn%20before%20it%2C%20as%20a%20dark%20odious%20smoke%20cloaked%20half%20the%20arena.%20Then%20the%20%3Ci%3Ecraftling%3C%2Fi%3E%20automaton%20emerged%20from%20the%20thick%20of%20the%20smoke%2C%20to%20the%20flank%20of%20its%20opponent.%20With%20its%20spin%20hammer%20it%20mangled%20loose%20a%20roller%20from%20its%20victim.%20Despite%20this%2C%20the%20drake%20automaton%20managed%20to%20come%20about%2C%20then%20struck%20back%20with%20its%20battering%20ram%20to%20crush%20its%20foe%E2%80%99s%20wielder%20chamber%2C%20along%20with%20the%20poor%20%3Ci%3Ecraftlings%3C%2Fi%3E%20inside.%5Cn%5CnIt%20seemed%20a%20fateful%20blow.%20Until%20the%20%3Ci%3Ecraftling%E2%80%99s%3C%2Fi%3E%20automaton%20rolled%20back%2C%20took%20aim%20with%20its%20fire%20staff%2C%20then%20shot%20loose%20the%20flame%20spitter%20from%20the%20drake%E2%80%99s.%20As%20their%20automaton%20caught%20fire%2C%20the%20clasher%20wielders%20emerged%20from%20within%20its%20wreckage.%20They%20went%20to%20the%20%3Ci%3Ecraftling%3C%2Fi%3E%20automaton%20to%20honor%20their%20victorious%20opponents.%20Yet%20no%20%3Ci%3Ecraftlings%3C%2Fi%3E%20emerged%20from%20it%20to%20receive%20their%20praise.%20Neither%20to%20gloat%20as%20%3Ci%3Ecraftlings%3C%2Fi%3E%20often%20do.%5Cn%5CnA%20%3Ci%3Ecraftling%3C%2Fi%3E%20runesmith%20strode%20onto%20the%20arena%2C%20laughing%20as%20he%20went.%20He%20told%20the%20bewildered%20clashers%20there%20was%20no%20one%20within%20his%20automaton%2C%20no%20one%20wielding%20its%20inner%20workings.%20By%20his%20glyph%E2%80%93making%20he%20had%20granted%20this%20thing%20a%20Will%20of%20its%20own.%20Turning%20again%20to%20the%20automaton%2C%20the%20clashers%20gave%20it%20a%20humble%20nod.%5Cn%5Cn%E2%80%95%20%2031st%20century%20of%20the%20Time%20of%20Legend%20%20%E2%80%95%22%7D%2C%22children%22%3A%5B%5D%7D%5D%7D",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("― The Contest of the Automata ― There was a rumbling in the distance. Puffs of smoke rose from beyond the horizon. Then slowly they appeared, two hulking metal champions. The drake automaton came first into view, as it was the swifter of the two. It bore a vague likeness to a <i>drakekin</i>, yet wingless, tailless. Below its four legs were rollers in place of feet. It breathed a menacing black smoke as its metal shell gleamed like golden sunlight. Then the <i>craftling</i> automaton came into view. Like its creators, it was smaller, slower. The rollers that carried it were covered by curious metal feet that turned to meet the ground as it went along. It breathed a fair, nigh cloudlike smoke. The automata took their places in the arena, facing each other. Their inner toolworks clamored ceaselessly. The call was given to begin the duel. With a deafening shriek, the drake automaton spat out walls of flame, as it lurched ahead. Even the sand seemed to burn before it, as a dark odious smoke cloaked half the arena. Then the <i>craftling</i> automaton emerged from the thick of the smoke, to the flank of its opponent. With its spin hammer it mangled loose a roller from its victim. Despite this, the drake automaton managed to come about, then struck back with its battering ram to crush its foe’s wielder chamber, along with the poor <i>craftlings</i> inside. It seemed a fateful blow. Until the <i>craftling’s</i> automaton rolled back, took aim with its fire staff, then shot loose the flame spitter from the drake’s. As their automaton caught fire, the clasher wielders emerged from within its wreckage. They went to the <i>craftling</i> automaton to honor their victorious opponents. Yet no <i>craftlings</i> emerged from it to receive their praise. Neither to gloat as <i>craftlings</i> often do. A <i>craftling</i> runesmith strode onto the arena, laughing as he went. He told the bewildered clashers there was no one within his automaton, no one wielding its inner workings. By his glyph–making he had granted this thing a Will of its own. Turning again to the automaton, the clashers gave it a humble nod. ― 31st century of the Time of Legend ―"),
          },
        ],
      },
